  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry conditions are expected to continue into the\nweekend. Fire weather concerns remain low. \n\nMid-level ridging will build over the Southeast into this\nevening and Thursday. The ridge will prevail Friday, then gradually\nweaken into the weekend. Surface High pressure will also \nprevail into the weekend, bringing dry conditions. Temperatures \nwill rebound on Thursday with highs back into the mid 80s, \ngradually rising into the upper 80s to lower 90s over the \nweekend. There are no fire weather concerns thanks to the recent\nactive pattern and well above normal rainfall in most \nlocations.",
